WHY THIS IS NOT THE REPOSITORY'S LICENCE
----------------------------------------

The code in this repository is Apache 2.0. Apache is written for code: its
patent grant and NOTICE machinery read oddly stretched over prose, and CC BY
4.0 is the convention for documentation.

The split is deliberate rather than an oversight, and it holds in the other
direction too. Heliograph Cloud is proprietary and its documentation is public
and CC BY 4.0 as well, in `heliograph-io/heliograph-cloud-docs`. The security
pages are the ones a buyer reads adversarially, and their whole argument is
that each claim is checkable without trusting us. A security page whose source
is private and takes no corrections is weaker for no gain.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER
------------------------

Code samples in these pages are Apache 2.0, the same as the rest of the
repository. Copy them without attribution obligations under CC BY.

The heliograph name and marks are not licensed by either. Apache 2.0 section 6
reserves trademark expressly, and CC BY 4.0 section 2(b)(2) says the same:
"No trademark or patent rights are granted under this Public License."
